        "original_id": "adacbac6-9040-5c6a-a17b-265a33d50d99",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ludwig van Beethoven, Heinrich Marschner\n- Works: Turkish March, \"The Elephant Never Forgets\", El Chavo del Ocho\n- Topics: German classical music, German opera, cover versions\n\nFacts:\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was baptised on 17 December 1770 and died on 26 March 1827.\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was a German composer and pianist.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was born on 16 August 1795 and died on 14 December 1861.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was regarded as the most important composer of German opera between Weber and Wagner.\n- The Turkish March, also called Marcia alla turca, is a well-known classical march theme by Ludwig van Beethoven.\n- \"The Elephant Never Forgets\" is a cover of Ludwig van Beethoven's Turkish March.\n- \"The Elephant Never Forgets\" was used as the theme song for El Chavo del Ocho.",
